1
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:12,033
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:32,933
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:35,600
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:41,467
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,467
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,467 --> 00:00:45,633
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,633 --> 00:00:46,767
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:49,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:51,500
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:53,600
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,633 --> 00:00:55,967
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,967 --> 00:00:58,500
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:00,800
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,633 --> 00:01:03,433
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,767 --> 00:01:06,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:09,933
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,533 --> 00:01:12,067
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:12,067 --> 00:01:13,667
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,667 --> 00:01:15,533
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,067 --> 00:01:21,833
<i>Are you going to attack
the NCIA?</i>

21
00:01:21,833 --> 00:01:23,367
<i> Kill or be killed.</i>

22
00:01:23,367 --> 00:01:24,533
<i> Pia's there.</i>

23
00:01:24,533 --> 00:01:27,400
<i>We're moving now
to take them down quicker!</i>

24
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:28,800
<i>Arturo, provide backup
for Lucas.</i>

25
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:31,867
<i>Pia, we will have
a tribute dinner for Sam.</i>

26
00:01:31,867 --> 00:01:32,900
<i> That's a great idea, sir.</i>

27
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:35,567
<i> Jacinto was a special agent.</i>

28
00:01:35,567 --> 00:01:37,533
<i>Thank you so, so much
for all your help!</i>

29
00:01:37,533 --> 00:01:38,867
<i> If it weren't for all of you,</i>

30
00:01:38,867 --> 00:01:41,500
<i>we wouldn't have defeated
and driven away our enemies.</i>

31
00:01:41,533 --> 00:01:43,400
<i>I hope you can also live
for Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

32
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,700
[CHANTING]  Gloria! Gloria!

33
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:46,033
<i>You have been
a great help to us.</i>

34
00:01:46,033 --> 00:01:47,433
<i>Thank you for having
a good heart.</i>

35
00:01:47,433 --> 00:01:48,767
<i> I love you so much, Gloria.</i>

36
00:01:48,767 --> 00:01:50,000
<i> So much.</i>

37
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,167
[CAR DOORS OPEN]

38
00:01:53,167 --> 00:02:00,167
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

39
00:02:05,533 --> 00:02:06,700
Any updates?

40
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:09,000
Security has tightened
at the NCIA, boss.

41
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,900
But if we want to,
we can easily attack the place.

42
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:15,167
No.

43
00:02:15,733 --> 00:02:17,067
They're definitely on alert

44
00:02:17,067 --> 00:02:19,067
because of
Samantha Jacinto's death.

45
00:02:19,867 --> 00:02:22,833
Let's wait until it gets dark
and there are fewer guards.

46
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:25,033
- Copy, boss.
- Okay, boss.

47
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:28,067
[LINE RINGING]

48
00:02:28,067 --> 00:02:29,633
[DEBORAH]
<i> What do you have for me?</i>

49
00:02:29,633 --> 00:02:30,967
[PIA]  Hello, ma'am.

50
00:02:30,967 --> 00:02:35,933
<i>The NCIA is holding an event
at a restaurant here.</i>

51
00:02:35,933 --> 00:02:37,733
Delgado will be there.

52
00:02:37,733 --> 00:02:41,900
Along with the agents
handling Victor's case

53
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:44,133
<i> and the case against you.</i>

54
00:02:44,133 --> 00:02:45,533
And?

55
00:02:45,533 --> 00:02:46,533
<i> If you want...</i>

56
00:02:46,533 --> 00:02:47,567
to take them out,

57
00:02:48,767 --> 00:02:49,900
come here.

58
00:02:50,833 --> 00:02:52,000
Where is it?

59
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,733
I'll send you the address later.

60
00:02:54,733 --> 00:02:56,133
But wait for my signal.

61
00:02:56,133 --> 00:02:59,600
I need to get out of here first
before you make your move.

62
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:01,033
Oh, of course.

63
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:05,567
You're our only connection
to the NCIA.

64
00:03:05,567 --> 00:03:08,033
We don't want anything
happening to you.

65
00:03:08,767 --> 00:03:10,100
Okay, I'll just call you later.

66
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:11,133
[DEBORAH]  Okay.

67
00:03:11,133 --> 00:03:12,800
Coordinate with Arturo.

68
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:15,000
He'll know what to do.

69
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,133
Alright, ma'am.

70
00:03:16,133 --> 00:03:20,000
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

71
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,800
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

72
00:03:22,833 --> 00:03:25,600
[VAN ENGINE HUMMING]

73
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:27,067
[VAN DOOR OPENS]

74
00:03:30,133 --> 00:03:31,233
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

75
00:03:33,133 --> 00:03:34,133
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

76
00:03:34,633 --> 00:03:36,600
- What are you doing here?
- Lucas...

77
00:03:38,700 --> 00:03:40,633
Papa really doesn't trust me,
does he?

78
00:03:41,267 --> 00:03:42,833
He actually sent a nanny
to watch me.

79
00:03:43,967 --> 00:03:47,500
Tell Papa I'm better than
his new pet.

80
00:03:47,867 --> 00:03:51,100
I'll prove to him
that I can think for myself.

81
00:03:51,833 --> 00:03:53,233
I have my own way
of doing things.

82
00:03:53,833 --> 00:03:55,800
And I don't just rush
into things.

83
00:03:55,833 --> 00:03:57,033
What's your plan?

84
00:03:57,033 --> 00:03:58,967
I don't need to explain
myself to you.

85
00:03:58,967 --> 00:04:02,667
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:04:02,667 --> 00:04:05,767
[PHONE RINGING]

87
00:04:06,233 --> 00:04:07,500
Hello, Ma.

88
00:04:07,833 --> 00:04:10,533
Lucas, where are you?

89
00:04:10,967 --> 00:04:12,833
Even you don't trust me?

90
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:14,967
Are you monitoring
my every move?

91
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:21,867
I already know where we're
going to attack the NCIA.

92
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,967
Pia already told me.

93
00:04:25,233 --> 00:04:27,700
<i>She's coordinating
with Arturo now.</i>

94
00:04:27,733 --> 00:04:31,267
So listen to
what Arturo tells you.

95
00:04:31,267 --> 00:04:33,067
Why Arturo?

96
00:04:33,067 --> 00:04:34,667
I know what I'm doing, Ma!

97
00:04:35,667 --> 00:04:39,033
What does your father
tell you every time?

98
00:04:39,033 --> 00:04:42,667
Every battle has
to be thought through.

99
00:04:42,667 --> 00:04:44,100
<i> It has to be planned.</i>

100
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:46,200
You can't just rush into things.

101
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,900
<i> Before every little move,</i>

102
00:04:50,367 --> 00:04:54,333
make sure you know
what you're getting into.

103
00:04:57,367 --> 00:04:58,567
Okay, Ma.

104
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:01,100
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

105
00:05:01,133 --> 00:05:03,033
I already know the location
of the restaurant.

106
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:06,233
Well, what are you waiting for?

107
00:05:06,233 --> 00:05:07,267
Move!

108
00:05:07,267 --> 00:05:08,567
- Let's go.
- Come on.

109
00:05:10,733 --> 00:05:12,900
[CAR ENGINE STARTS]

110
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:16,033
I just hope your son
doesn't mess this up.

111
00:05:17,633 --> 00:05:18,767
He won't.

112
00:05:18,767 --> 00:05:25,333
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

113
00:05:29,767 --> 00:05:32,700
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

114
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:37,067
Your late brother has something
he wants to tell you.

115
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:38,100
[GASP]

116
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:39,967
Oh, gosh! That's creepy.

117
00:05:39,967 --> 00:05:41,267
- Really?
- Mm.

118
00:05:41,267 --> 00:05:43,633
But my siblings are still alive.

119
00:05:43,633 --> 00:05:45,100
What about your father?

120
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:47,267
- Oh, he's the one who's dead.
- That's who I'm referring to.

121
00:05:47,267 --> 00:05:48,767
That's who we'll be talking to.

122
00:05:48,767 --> 00:05:52,633
Because he's the one
who'll explain to you

123
00:05:52,633 --> 00:05:55,900
about his illegitimate child

124
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:56,900
[GASP]

125
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:58,233
My goodness!

126
00:05:58,233 --> 00:05:59,900
- His illegitimate child?
- You have a half-sibling?

127
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:01,800
- [GASP]
- Goodness gracious!

128
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:04,133
- How remarkable!
- How did you know?

129
00:06:04,133 --> 00:06:05,767
Can you do me next,
Madam?

130
00:06:05,767 --> 00:06:07,933
- She's incredible.
- I think she's right.

131
00:06:07,967 --> 00:06:11,800
[ROSA]
Sir, investments are like life.

132
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:14,800
Sometimes you win,
sometimes you lose.

133
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:18,000
All right. Then, tell me
which of my business partners

134
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,433
is playing me dirty.

135
00:06:19,433 --> 00:06:24,133
[MYSTERIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

136
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:25,733
It's a man.

137
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:28,933
- It's a man.
- [CHUCKLES]

138
00:06:28,933 --> 00:06:30,867
- A man?
- She's right!

139
00:06:30,867 --> 00:06:32,400
All of my business partners
are men!

140
00:06:34,967 --> 00:06:36,667
But this business partner

141
00:06:36,667 --> 00:06:43,333
is the last person
you'd think would betray you.

142
00:06:43,367 --> 00:06:44,833
Oh, really? [SCOFFS]

143
00:06:44,833 --> 00:06:48,000
Here's what we're going to do.

144
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:51,167
I will come to your office.

145
00:06:51,167 --> 00:06:56,400
Then, I can personally
point out who it is.

146
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:57,767
- Mm!
- [SLAMS TABLE]

147
00:06:59,133 --> 00:07:00,400
[KNOCKS]

148
00:07:00,400 --> 00:07:01,800
Dad?

149
00:07:04,167 --> 00:07:06,900
I just wanted to
let you know that

150
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:08,700
I'm going back to work tomorrow.

151
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,100
Why? Uh...

152
00:07:12,333 --> 00:07:14,167
You can still extend your break.

153
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:16,733
Life goes on, right?

154
00:07:18,933 --> 00:07:22,200
I'm telling you this because
I'm worried about Mom.

155
00:07:23,867 --> 00:07:26,367
What'll happen when
it's just the two of you here?

156
00:07:27,933 --> 00:07:30,833
I don't think she's
handling this very well.

157
00:07:32,867 --> 00:07:36,200
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

158
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:37,333
Max.

159
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:40,467
[GRUNTS SOFTLY]

160
00:07:42,367 --> 00:07:45,367
Did you think this would
be easier for your mother

161
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:52,867
because she already
lost a child before?

162
00:07:52,867 --> 00:07:57,067
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

163
00:07:57,067 --> 00:07:58,867
Of course not, Dad.

164
00:07:59,967 --> 00:08:01,533
I'm just worried about her

165
00:08:01,533 --> 00:08:03,900
because she believes
in that psychic.

166
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:07,033
We both know she's a phony.

167
00:08:07,033 --> 00:08:08,933
But, Max...

168
00:08:09,967 --> 00:08:11,933
let's let her do
what she wants.

169
00:08:11,933 --> 00:08:14,900
As long as the psychic
isn't harming her...

170
00:08:17,033 --> 00:08:18,367
I'm fine with it.

171
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:21,933
Besides,
maybe this is her way...

172
00:08:23,133 --> 00:08:24,567
of finding peace.

173
00:08:25,833 --> 00:08:27,233
Let's give it to her.

174
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,033
Okay, Dad.

175
00:08:31,933 --> 00:08:35,233
That Madam Rosa
better not be up to no good.

176
00:08:36,933 --> 00:08:39,200
Because she will answer to me.

177
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:47,067
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

178
00:09:02,133 --> 00:09:09,067
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

179
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,567
[ISOBEL]  Sam...

180
00:09:16,967 --> 00:09:21,133
<i> Help us heal as a family.</i>

181
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,967
<i> I know it's hard...</i>

182
00:09:26,167 --> 00:09:28,133
<i> But we'll try.</i>

183
00:09:30,167 --> 00:09:34,533
<i>Mommy will do her best
to be strong... for you.</i>

184
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:39,433
<i> I love you, my dear.</i>

185
00:09:40,467 --> 00:09:42,200
<i> I love you.</i>

186
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:49,267
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

187
00:09:53,467 --> 00:09:55,767
[OLI] Hey, man, I'm sorry.
I got overwhelmed!

188
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:57,800
I got scared of the gun!

189
00:09:57,800 --> 00:10:00,000
That's the first time I came
face to face with Jacinto.

190
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,867
I risked my life, and you forgot
to turn on the camera?!

191
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:04,567
Are you stupid?!

192
00:10:04,567 --> 00:10:06,933
Hold on. Watch out how
you speak to me, man.

193
00:10:06,933 --> 00:10:10,533
I think you're forgetting
that I was there too!

194
00:10:10,533 --> 00:10:12,300
It was a mess out there,
Salvador!

195
00:10:12,567 --> 00:10:14,233
He threatened us, man,
he threatened us!

196
00:10:14,233 --> 00:10:17,500
And he'll take it seriously
if we won't stop targeting him!

197
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:19,200
I don't want to die, Salvador.

198
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,867
- [CHUCKLES]
- I'm still young!

199
00:10:20,867 --> 00:10:22,533
My kids are too young!

200
00:10:22,533 --> 00:10:23,767
Can he handle this fist?

201
00:10:23,767 --> 00:10:25,533
Can he? Huh?

202
00:10:25,533 --> 00:10:27,100
Do you see these fists?!

203
00:10:27,100 --> 00:10:30,000
I'll go even harder on him
in my next episode!

204
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,167
Fine, go ahead.

205
00:10:31,767 --> 00:10:34,100
Your first episode might
as well be your last.

206
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:35,900
Keep in mind, Salvador,

207
00:10:35,933 --> 00:10:39,067
that his daughter
was salvaged.

208
00:10:39,067 --> 00:10:41,433
He's still mentally out of it,
man. He's mourning.

209
00:10:41,433 --> 00:10:43,567
Next time, he might
have you assassinated.

210
00:10:44,033 --> 00:10:45,367
Do you think
he can do that?

211
00:10:45,367 --> 00:10:47,433
[CHUCKLES] Salvador.

212
00:10:47,433 --> 00:10:50,567
He was a General!

213
00:10:50,567 --> 00:10:52,600
What do you think
he did to those criminals

214
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:54,033
and those who made
him suffer?

215
00:10:54,033 --> 00:10:55,133
What do you think?

216
00:10:55,133 --> 00:10:57,933
Don't ever wish for
that to happen to you.

217
00:10:57,933 --> 00:10:59,200
- Do you understand?
- Yes.

218
00:10:59,900 --> 00:11:01,067
- Do you want that to happen?
- No.

219
00:11:02,533 --> 00:11:03,800
Put that in the bag.

220
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:05,200
- [TOTO] C'mon!
- Why won't you put it?

221
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:07,033
No one will eat this anyway!

222
00:11:07,033 --> 00:11:08,100
Is this yours?

223
00:11:08,133 --> 00:11:10,233
She'll entertain us for sure!

224
00:11:10,233 --> 00:11:11,967
C'mon, Toto,
this is embarrassing!

225
00:11:11,967 --> 00:11:13,400
- She might be tired.
- This is free, right?

226
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:15,267
She already entertained
a lot of people earlier.

227
00:11:15,267 --> 00:11:17,433
C'mon,
she'll entertain us for sure!

228
00:11:17,433 --> 00:11:19,333
Wait! She's taking
all the leftover food.

229
00:11:19,333 --> 00:11:21,600
- [MADAM ROSA] This one too.
- [CLEARS THROAT]

230
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:23,267
Madam Rosa?

231
00:11:23,267 --> 00:11:24,133
What is it?

232
00:11:24,133 --> 00:11:25,467
Why is she acting so snobby?

233
00:11:25,467 --> 00:11:28,567
Not a single warmth
to the non-rich.

234
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:30,467
Uh, Madam?

235
00:11:30,467 --> 00:11:32,467
Toto would just like
to have his fortune told.

236
00:11:33,967 --> 00:11:34,867
Are you done?

237
00:11:35,233 --> 00:11:36,933
Madam! Madam!

238
00:11:36,933 --> 00:11:39,833
I'll just ask for the lottery
numbers, that's it!

239
00:11:39,833 --> 00:11:42,167
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

240
00:11:42,200 --> 00:11:43,167
[GASPS]

241
00:11:43,167 --> 00:11:44,233
Madam!

242
00:11:45,167 --> 00:11:47,967
Are you already reading
Toto's future?

243
00:11:50,033 --> 00:11:51,467
- [TWINKLE EXCLAIMS]
- [TOTO CLEARS THROAT]

244
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:57,933
You won't get rich.

245
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:04,267
Even if your work yourself
to the bone,

246
00:12:04,267 --> 00:12:06,100
you won't get anywhere.

247
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:09,833
You will stay poor.

248
00:12:10,167 --> 00:12:11,333
Poor!

249
00:12:12,467 --> 00:12:13,467
Well? Give it to me!

250
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:15,300
- Is this all?
- Yes.

251
00:12:15,333 --> 00:12:16,400
Alright then.

252
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:18,133
Why does it seem so little.

253
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:31,200
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

254
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:32,633
[SOBBING]

255
00:12:39,367 --> 00:12:40,333
Ah.

256
00:12:40,667 --> 00:12:42,000
Madam Rosa.

257
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:44,967
[ISOBEL SIGHS]

258
00:12:44,967 --> 00:12:48,133
Thank you for letting me talk
to Samantha.

259
00:12:50,033 --> 00:12:51,000
ah, by the way,

260
00:12:52,233 --> 00:12:53,533
here's a little thank you.

261
00:12:59,533 --> 00:13:01,167
A little welcome to you, too.

262
00:13:02,167 --> 00:13:03,967
All right, ma'am, I'm leaving.

263
00:13:05,267 --> 00:13:06,333
Madam?

264
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:12,367
Can I get my daughter's
necklace back?

265
00:13:13,367 --> 00:13:15,167
Uh, Isobel...

266
00:13:15,167 --> 00:13:18,400
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

267
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:21,233
This is the connection
we'll have with Sam.

268
00:13:21,267 --> 00:13:24,400
It needs to be close
to Madam Rosa

269
00:13:24,400 --> 00:13:26,933
so we can talk to your daughter.

270
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:29,233
Do you not want
to talk to her anymore?

271
00:13:29,233 --> 00:13:30,600
No, I want to talk to her!

272
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:32,400
Okay, um...

273
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:34,233
Hold on to it.

274
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:36,967
I'm tired.

275
00:13:36,967 --> 00:13:41,600
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

276
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:43,100
[DOOR CLOSES]

277
00:13:43,100 --> 00:13:44,233
Oh, yes!

278
00:13:45,067 --> 00:13:46,400
You're really awesome!

279
00:13:47,033 --> 00:13:49,567
Your words
still work like magic!

280
00:13:49,567 --> 00:13:52,100
Well, would you look at that?

281
00:13:53,367 --> 00:13:54,500
This is great!

282
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,067
Very good, Madam.

283
00:13:57,067 --> 00:13:58,267
This will do.

284
00:13:58,267 --> 00:14:03,167
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

285
00:14:03,167 --> 00:14:05,633
Where did you learn that, huh?

286
00:14:05,633 --> 00:14:07,233
Whatever it is your doing.

287
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:09,300
This cannot be learned.

288
00:14:10,133 --> 00:14:13,433
It is a gift from the universe

289
00:14:13,433 --> 00:14:16,300
that only Madam Rosa
has been blessed with

290
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:18,167
when she was born with

291
00:14:18,167 --> 00:14:20,133
her umbilical cord wrapped
around her head.

292
00:14:23,633 --> 00:14:24,733
Wait.

293
00:14:27,733 --> 00:14:30,267
You're wearing Sam's necklace.

294
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:33,467
Your mother knows this.
I have her permission.

295
00:14:33,467 --> 00:14:34,667
Mind your own business.

296
00:14:35,633 --> 00:14:37,167
I know what you're doing.

297
00:14:37,167 --> 00:14:38,633
I can smell it.

298
00:14:40,167 --> 00:14:41,800
Just don't let me catch you,

299
00:14:42,833 --> 00:14:45,033
because it'll come back
to you tenfold.

300
00:14:45,033 --> 00:14:46,767
Even if karma comes
back and forth

301
00:14:46,767 --> 00:14:49,333
you won't catch Madam Rosa

302
00:14:49,333 --> 00:14:52,200
because she didn't do
anything wrong.

303
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:53,200
[HUFFS] Hmph!

304
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:59,300
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING,
FADES]

305
00:15:00,133 --> 00:15:01,133
[GABO] Auntie?

306
00:15:01,133 --> 00:15:03,033
- [MAMENG] Hmm?
- What's for dinner?

307
00:15:03,067 --> 00:15:06,200
Well, of course,
just like always,

308
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:07,500
- sardines!
- [GABO] Wow.

309
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:09,367
- [CHUCKLES]
- But to change it up,

310
00:15:09,367 --> 00:15:11,700
we'll add it
to the wheat noodle soup.

311
00:15:11,700 --> 00:15:13,133
That's delicious.

312
00:15:13,133 --> 00:15:14,500
That's perfect.
I'm so exhausted.

313
00:15:14,867 --> 00:15:17,367
I was just thinking, Gabo,

314
00:15:17,367 --> 00:15:20,633
maybe God really intended
for this job hunt of yours--

315
00:15:20,633 --> 00:15:23,300
your job applications
to not push through.

316
00:15:23,833 --> 00:15:25,167
What do you mean, babes?

317
00:15:25,567 --> 00:15:27,733
If Gabo completely leaves,

318
00:15:27,733 --> 00:15:29,333
who's going to defend us?

319
00:15:29,333 --> 00:15:31,400
Most likely, a lot
of people here get hurt,

320
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:32,567
just like Babot and the others.

321
00:15:32,567 --> 00:15:35,267
[RUDY] You have a point, Mameng.

322
00:15:35,867 --> 00:15:37,833
If Gabo hadn't gone there,

323
00:15:37,833 --> 00:15:40,367
they probably would have killed
the people there.

324
00:15:40,733 --> 00:15:42,733
[DANTE] Wait,
who are they anyway?

325
00:15:42,733 --> 00:15:44,167
Who else?

326
00:15:44,167 --> 00:15:47,733
I'm pretty sure it's
Ricardo Jacinto's people.

327
00:15:47,733 --> 00:15:53,833
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

328
00:15:53,833 --> 00:15:56,367
Maybe... they aren't.

329
00:15:56,833 --> 00:15:59,367
Maybe this is what Sir Babot's
wife was talking about.

330
00:15:59,733 --> 00:16:02,533
They mentioned to me
that they were kidnapped before

331
00:16:02,533 --> 00:16:04,300
to extract
their internal organs.

332
00:16:05,233 --> 00:16:06,700
[RUDY] No, it's not like that.

333
00:16:06,833 --> 00:16:09,533
Ricardo Jacinto
ordered those people

334
00:16:09,567 --> 00:16:12,400
to take our land away.

335
00:16:12,733 --> 00:16:14,233
[CHAIR CLATTERS]

336
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:17,700
But, Pa...

337
00:16:18,767 --> 00:16:21,700
we can't just accuse people
carelessly.

338
00:16:22,233 --> 00:16:24,700
We don't know
who those people are.

339
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:28,367
They could have a different
reason for being here.

340
00:16:28,367 --> 00:16:31,633
Still, Gabo, we need
to remain vigilant.

341
00:16:31,633 --> 00:16:33,433
What if they come back?

342
00:16:33,433 --> 00:16:36,933
I can assure you, you'll be
the first person they'll target.

343
00:16:36,933 --> 00:16:38,200
Trust me.

344
00:16:38,433 --> 00:16:39,567
But, wow.

345
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:41,433
you're amazing.

346
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:44,933
You sent those people packing!

347
00:16:44,933 --> 00:16:47,833
Our fellow townspeople
can't help but look up at you!

348
00:16:47,833 --> 00:16:51,533
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

349
00:16:51,767 --> 00:16:53,767
[SAM] <i> I don't know
</i> who they are too.

350
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:57,767
<i>But I'm sure Daddy isn't
capable of doing such a thing.</i>

351
00:16:59,333 --> 00:17:01,800
<i> To kill someone helpless.</i>

352
00:17:01,800 --> 00:17:02,767
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

353
00:17:04,967 --> 00:17:05,967
[VEHICLES APPROACHING]

354
00:17:11,067 --> 00:17:12,933
[TIRES SCREECH]

355
00:17:15,133 --> 00:17:17,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

356
00:17:17,333 --> 00:17:20,433
This is the restaurant
Ms. Catacutan mentioned.

357
00:17:20,433 --> 00:17:22,800
What are we waiting for?

358
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:27,300
Why don't we open fire
the moment they arrive?

359
00:17:27,300 --> 00:17:28,433
Your mother's order

360
00:17:28,433 --> 00:17:30,800
is to wait for
Ms. Catacutan's go signal.

361
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:32,533
Do you really think
I'm going to listen to you?

362
00:17:32,533 --> 00:17:37,667
I'm not going to let some woman
make my decisions for me.

363
00:17:37,667 --> 00:17:41,533
Lucas, we need teamwork
in operations like this.

364
00:17:41,533 --> 00:17:42,867
Ms. Catacutan
is our person inside,

365
00:17:42,867 --> 00:17:45,267
so she knows their movements.

366
00:17:45,267 --> 00:17:47,267
Tell her
I want to talk to her.

367
00:17:47,267 --> 00:17:50,633
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

368
00:17:50,667 --> 00:17:53,533
[KEYPAD CLACKING]

369
00:17:53,533 --> 00:17:55,200
- Put that over there! Hurry!
- Okay, ma'am.

370
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:56,667
Pick up the pace!

371
00:17:58,467 --> 00:17:59,433
Father!

372
00:18:00,633 --> 00:18:01,767
Uh...

373
00:18:02,733 --> 00:18:04,467
We weren't expecting you
till later.

374
00:18:04,467 --> 00:18:06,333
Yes, well,
there wasn't any traffic.

375
00:18:06,333 --> 00:18:09,200
Is that so? Would you like
something to eat?

376
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:10,633
We're good. Thank you.

377
00:18:10,633 --> 00:18:12,633
- Uh, Ace?
- Yes, ma'am?

378
00:18:12,633 --> 00:18:14,667
Could you assist Father?

379
00:18:14,667 --> 00:18:16,167
No problem.
Father, this way.

380
00:18:16,167 --> 00:18:17,433
Thank you.

381
00:18:18,667 --> 00:18:20,200
[PHONE CHIMES]

382
00:18:20,867 --> 00:18:22,633
[ARTURO] "We're outside.
Lucas wants to speak to you."

383
00:18:22,667 --> 00:18:29,567
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

384
00:18:32,767 --> 00:18:34,333
- Good evening, Ma'am Pia.
- Sorry we're late.

385
00:18:34,333 --> 00:18:35,900
It's okay. Go inside.

386
00:18:35,900 --> 00:18:42,833
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

387
00:18:57,900 --> 00:18:59,300
They're on the way.

388
00:18:59,300 --> 00:19:02,700
Wait an hour before you attack.
All right?

389
00:19:02,700 --> 00:19:05,700
The NCIA director will be there.

390
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:09,567
Samantha Jacinto's team
will also be there.

391
00:19:09,567 --> 00:19:11,233
They're the ones
who captured my brother.

392
00:19:11,633 --> 00:19:14,700
They will also file a case
against your family.

393
00:19:14,700 --> 00:19:16,367
That's not going to happen.

394
00:19:16,367 --> 00:19:19,733
They will have a reunion with
Samantha Jacinto in hell.

395
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:24,367
Remember, don't do anything
unless I tell you to.

396
00:19:24,867 --> 00:19:26,367
What time do you have
on your clocks?

397
00:19:26,933 --> 00:19:28,900
We need to have the same time.

398
00:19:29,933 --> 00:19:31,267
An hour.

399
00:19:31,267 --> 00:19:32,733
Give me an hour.

400
00:19:32,733 --> 00:19:34,467
I'm just going to fix this.

401
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:36,433
Also,

402
00:19:36,433 --> 00:19:38,967
Sebastian shouldn't get
caught up in this.

403
00:19:39,667 --> 00:19:41,733
I don't care who gets involved.

404
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:43,633
An hour.

405
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:46,300
Exactly one hour.

406
00:19:46,300 --> 00:19:47,600
Then we'll attack.

407
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:52,633
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

408
00:19:52,633 --> 00:19:53,600
An hour.

409
00:19:55,733 --> 00:20:02,700
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

410
00:20:04,667 --> 00:20:05,733
Here they come.

411
00:20:09,033 --> 00:20:10,000
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

412
00:20:17,867 --> 00:20:20,000
What took you so long?
You took forever!

413
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,000
[PIA] Everything is
ready in there!

414
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,533
You guys took a long time!
I've been here for a while!

415
00:20:23,533 --> 00:20:25,300
We had some things
to finish, ma'am.

416
00:20:26,933 --> 00:20:28,633
We were also waiting for
Sir Delgado.

417
00:20:28,633 --> 00:20:30,767
He's on his way.
Oh, here they are.

418
00:20:30,767 --> 00:20:31,733
Miss Pia.

419
00:20:32,933 --> 00:20:36,000
[CAR APPROACHING]

420
00:20:37,733 --> 00:20:39,133
[PIA] Sir, good evening.

421
00:20:39,133 --> 00:20:40,000
Good evening.

422
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,433
This way.

423
00:20:41,967 --> 00:20:42,933
Thank you.

424
00:20:48,467 --> 00:20:54,800
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

425
00:20:55,133 --> 00:20:56,333
[ELTON] We've been here
since this morning!

426
00:20:56,333 --> 00:20:57,533
It's already nighttime!

427
00:20:58,133 --> 00:21:01,567
Sir Elton, Gabo suddenly
got into a fight.

428
00:21:01,567 --> 00:21:03,967
And now, it's already night!

429
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:06,900
[DIDAY] Gabo is
really good, right?

430
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:08,633
It's a shame we didn't see it!

431
00:21:08,667 --> 00:21:10,833
Have you seen
Gabo holding a gun?

432
00:21:10,833 --> 00:21:12,000
He looks so trained!

433
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:13,933
Mom, have you forgotten
where Gabo came from?

434
00:21:13,933 --> 00:21:15,167
In prison!

435
00:21:15,167 --> 00:21:17,433
You know, ever since
he was a young boy,

436
00:21:17,433 --> 00:21:19,067
he is used to trouble.

437
00:21:19,067 --> 00:21:21,667
Fistfights are nothing to him!

438
00:21:21,667 --> 00:21:24,167
Luckily, Gabo
and his friends came.

439
00:21:24,167 --> 00:21:25,733
If not, Babot would be dead!

440
00:21:25,733 --> 00:21:27,900
They pointed a gun
at him and beat him!

441
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:30,667
Gabo wouldn't have
let that happen!

442
00:21:30,667 --> 00:21:33,000
Good thing, Gabo's got you.

443
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,467
Miss Diday!

444
00:21:36,667 --> 00:21:38,500
You are really impressed
with Gabo, aren't you?

445
00:21:38,500 --> 00:21:41,733
Absolutely! Gabo's good
and so brave!

446
00:21:41,767 --> 00:21:43,867
Not a hint of fear
from him! Like me!

447
00:21:43,867 --> 00:21:45,933
Luckily, Gabo was here.

448
00:21:45,933 --> 00:21:48,967
Gabo really is our protector
here in Ginintuang Lupa.

449
00:21:48,967 --> 00:21:51,900
Especially from
Paquito and his son!

450
00:21:51,900 --> 00:21:53,767
- Django!
- Django, yes!

451
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:56,700
- Auntie, it smells good!
- Right?

452
00:21:56,700 --> 00:21:58,533
Of course! How about you?

453
00:21:58,533 --> 00:22:01,367
Do you eat sardines with  misua?

454
00:22:02,633 --> 00:22:03,800
Of course!

455
00:22:03,800 --> 00:22:06,700
We used to
eat this a lot in prison!

456
00:22:06,700 --> 00:22:08,533
This is Gloria's favorite!

457
00:22:08,533 --> 00:22:11,433
Good thing I cooked this!

458
00:22:11,433 --> 00:22:12,600
- [CHUCKLES]
- Here.

459
00:22:13,067 --> 00:22:14,600
Here, here, here.

460
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:15,933
Your turn now.

461
00:22:15,967 --> 00:22:17,067
[ELTON] Gabo! Gabo!

462
00:22:18,067 --> 00:22:20,067
Gabo, you know,

463
00:22:20,067 --> 00:22:22,000
the people outside are still
having a commotion over you!

464
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:24,667
You're the center of attention!
Everyone is talking about you!

465
00:22:24,667 --> 00:22:26,100
They were saying that
if you hadn't arrived earlier,

466
00:22:26,100 --> 00:22:27,733
a lot of people would have died.

467
00:22:28,733 --> 00:22:31,500
Elton, I've been doing that
even before.

468
00:22:31,500 --> 00:22:32,733
You know that...

469
00:22:32,733 --> 00:22:34,633
I'm not going to let
anyone in our area

470
00:22:34,633 --> 00:22:35,767
get hurt or be put to danger.

471
00:22:36,433 --> 00:22:37,800
You know what, Elton,

472
00:22:37,800 --> 00:22:39,067
this son of mine,

473
00:22:39,067 --> 00:22:41,833
even if he's a bit of
a troublemaker,

474
00:22:41,833 --> 00:22:43,767
even if people
see him as the bad guy,

475
00:22:44,067 --> 00:22:46,067
I am sure,

476
00:22:46,067 --> 00:22:47,567
that his heart is broken.

477
00:22:48,600 --> 00:22:51,067
[MAMENG] Did you hear that,
Gloria? Oh my!

478
00:22:51,533 --> 00:22:53,100
You're so lucky,

479
00:22:53,100 --> 00:22:56,000
our Gabo is so kind.

480
00:22:56,800 --> 00:22:58,200
[DANTE] Not just that.

481
00:22:58,200 --> 00:22:59,600
He's strong.

482
00:22:59,600 --> 00:23:01,700
No one can bully him!

483
00:23:01,700 --> 00:23:04,533
Even Paquito and Django?

484
00:23:04,533 --> 00:23:06,000
They're nothing to him!

485
00:23:07,533 --> 00:23:09,567
Gabo. Have you always
been like that?

486
00:23:10,933 --> 00:23:12,100
[GABO] Uhm.

487
00:23:12,100 --> 00:23:13,667
You know, love,

488
00:23:13,667 --> 00:23:15,000
here in our area,

489
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:17,767
you have to be brave
in order to live.

490
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:23,433
[SAMANTHA] <i> This is the first
</i>time I've seen a man like this.

491
00:23:24,067 --> 00:23:26,933
<i>He's willing to sacrifice
his life for others.</i>

492
00:23:29,800 --> 00:23:31,200
Love.

493
00:23:31,200 --> 00:23:33,133
Here, take a bite.

494
00:23:33,133 --> 00:23:35,633
- [CHUCKLES]
- That's your favorite.

495
00:23:35,633 --> 00:23:37,700
- Good?
- Hey, invite him to eat!

496
00:23:37,700 --> 00:23:39,133
- [GABO LAUGHS]
- Elton!

497
00:23:39,133 --> 00:23:42,133
- Take a seat!
- You're waiting to be invited!

498
00:23:42,133 --> 00:23:46,233
[MAMENG] Get a plate
and utensils for Elton.

499
00:23:46,233 --> 00:23:48,500
- [DANTE] Here, Elton.
- Auntie's cooking is good!

500
00:23:48,500 --> 00:23:49,800
Here, here, here.

501
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:50,867
Oh, thank you.

502
00:23:52,133 --> 00:23:53,533
You know, Gloria,

503
00:23:54,500 --> 00:23:56,633
I thought Gabo
is so lucky to have you

504
00:23:56,667 --> 00:23:59,200
because you're beautiful
and smart!

505
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:01,567
Turns out, you're lucky
to have Gabo too.

506
00:24:02,167 --> 00:24:03,567
Do you know why?

507
00:24:03,567 --> 00:24:04,933
He's very brave.

508
00:24:04,933 --> 00:24:08,167
He can protect you from anyone!

509
00:24:08,700 --> 00:24:10,567
I hope, Gloria,

510
00:24:10,567 --> 00:24:12,600
you two would have
a lot of children.

511
00:24:12,600 --> 00:24:13,733
[MAMENG] Oh gosh!

512
00:24:13,733 --> 00:24:16,667
I do hope they'll have
a lot of children!

513
00:24:16,667 --> 00:24:19,233
Because I am sure that
their children will be

514
00:24:19,233 --> 00:24:22,900
good-looking and kind.

515
00:24:23,100 --> 00:24:24,500
Son, you know,

516
00:24:25,100 --> 00:24:27,267
honestly, if you'll
have a child,

517
00:24:27,267 --> 00:24:31,033
I'll be the happiest
grandfather in the world!

518
00:24:31,067 --> 00:24:33,767
I'll be proud
of my grandchildren.

519
00:24:33,767 --> 00:24:34,933
[MAMENG] Mmm.

520
00:24:35,600 --> 00:24:40,033
Love, you're
hearing them, right?

521
00:24:40,633 --> 00:24:43,600
They want us to
have a lot of children.

522
00:24:43,867 --> 00:24:45,000
Perhaps...

523
00:24:45,767 --> 00:24:48,900
later, after taking a bath,

524
00:24:49,267 --> 00:24:51,100
we can start
making a lot of babies.

525
00:24:51,100 --> 00:24:53,200
[LAUGHTER]

526
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:55,667
[MAMENG] This kid is so naughty!

527
00:24:55,933 --> 00:24:57,867
- [LAUGHTER]
- Oh my, Gabo.

528
00:24:57,867 --> 00:24:59,067
- There!
- I think later

529
00:24:59,067 --> 00:25:00,767
will be a good night!

530
00:25:00,767 --> 00:25:04,667
[LAUGHTER]

531
00:25:04,967 --> 00:25:06,700
[MAMENG] You're silly, Gabo!

532
00:25:07,400 --> 00:25:08,900
[GROWLING] Argh!

533
00:25:08,900 --> 00:25:12,200
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

534
00:25:15,600 --> 00:25:16,900
I'm stuffed!

535
00:25:16,900 --> 00:25:18,767
Your cooking is amazing, Mameng.
Thanks for the meal!

536
00:25:18,767 --> 00:25:20,500
Why, thank you.

537
00:25:20,500 --> 00:25:23,767
You can all go ahead.
I'll take care of this.

538
00:25:23,767 --> 00:25:26,567
- You may all go.
- [SAM] Join them, Gabo.

539
00:25:26,567 --> 00:25:27,933
Mameng and I
will take care of it.

540
00:25:27,933 --> 00:25:29,467
Okay, Love.

541
00:25:30,067 --> 00:25:31,167
[GABO GRUNTS]

542
00:25:31,167 --> 00:25:32,633
- [CLATTERING]
- The food was delicious!

543
00:25:32,633 --> 00:25:35,200
[DOOR CREAKING OPEN]

544
00:25:35,600 --> 00:25:38,100
[EXCLAIMS] Mameng's cooking
is the best!

545
00:25:38,100 --> 00:25:39,800
- I'm so full!
- That's for sure!

546
00:25:39,800 --> 00:25:41,767
It's my wife's cooking
after all!

547
00:25:41,767 --> 00:25:42,833
It's delicious!

548
00:25:42,833 --> 00:25:45,133
- [GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [DOOR CLOSES]

549
00:25:45,133 --> 00:25:46,600
- Auntie?
- Hm?

550
00:25:46,600 --> 00:25:50,467
Where did Mama Betchay
go earlier?

551
00:25:51,700 --> 00:25:55,467
Where else? The bar of course!
She works there.

552
00:25:57,600 --> 00:26:00,900
I just noticed that... she
seemed so happy earlier.

553
00:26:01,533 --> 00:26:03,533
Looks like she was
in a good mood.

554
00:26:03,533 --> 00:26:06,533
Try to get used to her.
You know how Betchay is.

555
00:26:06,533 --> 00:26:08,200
Her mood swings are drastic.

556
00:26:08,200 --> 00:26:10,900
She'll have an attitude
one moment.

557
00:26:11,133 --> 00:26:13,800
Then the next, she'll be sassy.

558
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:16,633
Aren't-- Aren't those two
the same?

559
00:26:16,633 --> 00:26:22,133
Exactly. You know, Betchay
says nothing good about us

560
00:26:22,133 --> 00:26:25,300
so whatever your hear
or see from her,

561
00:26:25,300 --> 00:26:27,000
just bear with it.

562
00:26:27,633 --> 00:26:29,833
Don't worry about me.

563
00:26:29,833 --> 00:26:33,667
I'll do everything to be able
to get along with her.

564
00:26:34,867 --> 00:26:38,067
You know, Gloria, I'm grateful

565
00:26:38,067 --> 00:26:40,300
for all that you do
because I can see

566
00:26:40,300 --> 00:26:44,933
that you can truly endure
and do everything for Gabo.

567
00:26:46,600 --> 00:26:48,733
I hope you two stay together
for a long time.

568
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:51,000
- I'm sorry?
- Oh...

569
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:52,533
I mean, uh...

570
00:26:52,533 --> 00:26:54,833
I hope you have lots of children
together.

571
00:26:55,700 --> 00:26:56,933
- Oh...
- [MAMENG] Ah!

572
00:26:56,933 --> 00:26:59,667
- Come on, let's clean up.
- A-- Alright. [LAUGHS]

573
00:26:59,667 --> 00:27:05,867
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

574
00:27:07,333 --> 00:27:08,567
[RUDY] Son.

575
00:27:08,700 --> 00:27:09,800
I hope...

576
00:27:10,600 --> 00:27:12,667
you don't do that again.

577
00:27:14,167 --> 00:27:16,233
Because, what if...

578
00:27:17,100 --> 00:27:18,667
you got shot back there?

579
00:27:19,033 --> 00:27:21,600
Or what if those guys
killed you?

580
00:27:21,600 --> 00:27:23,600
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

581
00:27:23,600 --> 00:27:24,533
Rudy.

582
00:27:25,067 --> 00:27:26,867
Don't blame it on Gabo.

583
00:27:27,933 --> 00:27:30,200
If not him, who will defend us
against them?

584
00:27:31,967 --> 00:27:33,900
Sure, I get that.

585
00:27:33,900 --> 00:27:36,100
My son is our defender.

586
00:27:36,100 --> 00:27:38,733
But what if... he gets
into trouble.

587
00:27:38,733 --> 00:27:41,000
He gets shot
like what happened to me.

588
00:27:41,800 --> 00:27:43,200
[SIGHS] You know, Gabo,

589
00:27:43,200 --> 00:27:46,033
you should learn to cool
your head.

590
00:27:46,033 --> 00:27:47,167
And...

591
00:27:47,900 --> 00:27:50,800
choose your battles.

592
00:27:50,833 --> 00:27:53,767
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

593
00:27:53,767 --> 00:27:54,733
Pa.

594
00:27:57,100 --> 00:27:58,300
I'm sorry.

595
00:27:58,833 --> 00:28:02,767
I'm really trying
to turn over a new leaf.

596
00:28:03,733 --> 00:28:06,633
But I can't resist helping
our fellow townspeople.

597
00:28:07,333 --> 00:28:08,300
[MOUTH SMACKS]

598
00:28:08,300 --> 00:28:09,967
But don't worry, Pa.

599
00:28:11,300 --> 00:28:12,967
I swear to you.

600
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:16,067
I'll really change my life.

601
00:28:17,167 --> 00:28:18,833
For Gloria.

602
00:28:18,833 --> 00:28:25,767
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

603
00:28:28,100 --> 00:28:29,267
Oh, Pa,

604
00:28:30,133 --> 00:28:31,667
I'll head inside.

605
00:28:31,667 --> 00:28:34,767
Uh, I'll lend Gloria
and Auntie a hand.

606
00:28:34,967 --> 00:28:36,000
- Sure, son.
- Sir.

607
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:37,100
Alright.

608
00:28:37,100 --> 00:28:39,300
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

609
00:28:39,300 --> 00:28:40,400
[CLEARS THROAT]

610
00:28:40,767 --> 00:28:43,367
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

611
00:28:43,367 --> 00:28:44,800
[GABO]  I feel sorry for her.

612
00:28:46,767 --> 00:28:49,100
<i>She doesn't deserve to go
through all of this.</i>

613
00:28:51,833 --> 00:28:53,600
<i> But I can't do anything.</i>

614
00:28:55,833 --> 00:28:57,967
<i> Her life is still in danger.</i>

615
00:29:00,467 --> 00:29:02,100
<i> But here in our house,</i>

616
00:29:04,300 --> 00:29:06,733
I can make sure that she's safe.

617
00:29:06,733 --> 00:29:13,633
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

618
00:29:19,300 --> 00:29:21,633
We could've been happy together.

619
00:29:21,633 --> 00:29:23,567
<i>It's such a shame
that you left us too soon.</i>

620
00:29:23,567 --> 00:29:25,733
<i>I couldn't even
let you experience</i>

621
00:29:25,733 --> 00:29:28,467
<i>how it feels to have
the best boyfriend ever.</i>

622
00:29:28,500 --> 00:29:29,533
<i> For Sam!</i>

623
00:29:29,533 --> 00:29:30,700
<i>- For Sam.
- For Sam!</i>

624
00:29:30,700 --> 00:29:34,367
- [RAPID GUNFIRE]
- [BULLETS RICOCHETING]

625
00:29:34,367 --> 00:29:36,533
<i>Though my memories
are yet to return,</i>

626
00:29:36,533 --> 00:29:38,533
<i>all I know is that you're
a great person.</i>

627
00:29:38,533 --> 00:29:40,333
<i> I'm sure of it.</i>

628
00:29:40,333 --> 00:29:41,833
<i>Do you know
why I invited you to drink?</i>

629
00:29:41,833 --> 00:29:43,267
<i>Because I wanted
to tell you something.</i>

630
00:29:43,267 --> 00:29:44,333
<i> What is it?</i>
